      "description": "Watch Feyenoord vs ADO Den Haag highlights and goals from Eredivisie on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 30, 2026. Feyenoord and ADO Den Haag played out a pulsating encounter at De Kuip as the Eredivisie season provided another chapter of high-octane football. With 47,500 fans in attendance on August 30, 2026 , the atmosphere was set for a dramatic afternoon that lived up to every expectation. ADO Stun the Home Crowd The visitors wasted no time in making their mark. In the 12th minute, Nigel Thomas produced a moment of brilliance, firing a right-footed shot from outside the box into the back of the net following an assist by Evan Rottier . Feyenoord struggled to find their rhythm in the immediate aftermath, despite the creative efforts of Gjivai Zechiel , who delivered several dangerous corners. The first half remained a frustrating affair for the hosts as they dominated the ball but failed to breach a disciplined ADO Den Haag defense. Second Half Turmoil and the Fightback The restart brought immediate drama as Sem Steijn struck the post for the visitors just moments into the second half. That warning went unheeded, and in the 53rd minute, Sekou Sylla doubled the lead for ADO Den Haag with a precise finish, assisted by Nigel Thomas . The tension at De Kuip reached a boiling point when a VAR review for a potential Feyenoord penalty was dismissed by the referee, leaving the home side with a mountain to climb. Refusing to buckle, Feyenoord finally found a lifeline in the 62nd minute. Ayase Ueda clinical finish from an Oussama Targhalline pass ignited the comeback. The pressure became relentless; after Anis Hadj Moussa hit the woodwork in the 70th minute, he made amends just two minutes later, slotting home the equalizer after being set up by Sem Steijn to bring the scores level at 2-2. A Tense Finale The closing stages were characterized by total Feyenoord control, as they finished the match with 69% possession. Substitutes like Nacho Ferri and Charles Vanhoutte tried to carve out a winner, but the visitors held firm. Even as Sem Steijn forced a save in the dying minutes and Mika Marmol sent a shot wide, the deadlock could not be broken. The final whistle confirmed a hard-fought draw, leaving both sides with plenty to reflect on from a captivating contest."
